EPANET 2.2 — network models and reproducible analysis (@wu-epanet: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_4D17YBA2R37W31ZCW7W54EDMWW
US EPA, EPANET 2.2, released July 2020. [Official software, source and manuals](https://www.epa.gov/water-research/epanet) · [Online manual](https://usepa.github.io/EPANET2.2/).

Work the complete quick-start tutorial, then read chapters 3, 8, 9 and 12 for model components, analysis settings, result interpretation and algorithms. Continue through the manual and file-format reference when constructing a reproducible network. Pin the executable/source revision and save inputs, units, controls, time settings and reports. The current cited manual is 2.2; extensions and community releases have their own versions.

Official pages and those chapters were inspected on 30 October 2026. EPA distributes source and executable downloads publicly. Inspect the selected release's licence and dependency notices before redistribution; this Record references the project and does not bundle it. A numerical network result is conditional on its topology, parameters, demands and controls; calibration and independent observations remain necessary.
} r_4D17YBA2R37W31ZCW7W54EDMWW
